Here are both approaches for navigating to `ProductDetailsPage` and receiving data via `IQueryAttributable`:

## 1. Register the Route

```csharp
// AppShell.xaml.cs
public AppShell()
{
    InitializeComponent();
    Routing.RegisterRoute("productdetails", typeof(ProductDetailsPage));
}
```

## 2. Navigate from ProductListPage

**Approach A — String query parameter (product ID only):**

```csharp
// In ProductListViewModel or code-behind
async void OnProductSelected(Product product)
{
    await Shell.Current.GoToAsync($"productdetails?productId={product.Id}");
}
```

**Approach B — Full object via `ShellNavigationQueryParameters`:**

```csharp
async void OnProductSelected(Product product)
{
    var parameters = new ShellNavigationQueryParameters
    {
        { "product", product }
    };
    await Shell.Current.GoToAsync("productdetails", parameters);
}
```

## 3. Receive Data on the ViewModel

```csharp
public class ProductDetailsViewModel : ObservableObject, IQueryAttributable
{
    private string _productId;
    private Product _product;

    public string ProductId
    {
        get => _productId;
        set => SetProperty(ref _productId, value);
    }

    public Product Product
    {
        get => _product;
        set => SetProperty(ref _product, value);
    }

    public void ApplyQueryAttributes(IDictionary<string, object> query)
    {
        // Approach A: string parameter from query string
        if (query.TryGetValue("productId", out var id))
        {
            ProductId = id.ToString();
            // Load full product from a service if needed
        }

        // Approach B: full object passed via ShellNavigationQueryParameters
        if (query.TryGetValue("product", out var obj) && obj is Product product)
        {
            Product = product;
            ProductId = product.Id;
        }
    }
}
```

## 4. Wire ViewModel to Page

```csharp
public partial class ProductDetailsPage : ContentPage
{
    public ProductDetailsPage(ProductDetailsViewModel vm)
    {
        InitializeComponent();
        BindingContext = vm;
    }
}
```

**Key differences:**

| | Query string | ShellNavigationQueryParameters |
|---|---|---|
| Data type | Strings only | Any object |
| Serialization | Manual (`ToString`) | None needed |
| URL-visible | Yes | No |
| Use when | Simple IDs/flags | Complex objects |

Both approaches deliver data to the same `ApplyQueryAttributes` method — you can even support both simultaneously as shown above.
